In article <1991Sep7.134107.13223@yang.earlham.edu> irac@yang.earlham.edu writes:
>Are there any disadvantages to appling a figurine and 
>producing the thing as a pet?
>also how does one kill killer bees?
>I am having trouble getting rid of them and they keep
>on knocking off my character.

I don't think this is considered as a spoiler, but I'll be safe.

Well, if it is cursed, it will become a monster, not your pet.  But other
than that, why not?  It really depends on your game plan, how much you use
the pet.  I often find pets very annoying, because he always eats juicy
corps and gets hungry way too often.  After I use him to rob a shop at the
lower level, I don't really care about him.  Still, I don't see any minuses
for creating a pet.  I don't think there is any penalty for abandoning a
pet. Could there be any potentially dangerous pets? (floating eye, medusa
maybe?)  It is always safer to identify things, of course.

You will meet killer bees at around level 10(?)  You should really have
poison resistant by that time, or you will be in trouble sooner or later.
Barbarians are poison resistant from the start, and there are amulet of
versus poison and ring of poison resistant.  If you have a potion of
restoration (or whatever), eat poisonous corpses and than drink the potion.
There maybe poison-resistant armors, but you should really have an
intrinsic.  If you are poison resistant and wearing a pretty good armor,
just line them up, and use your favorite method to kill 'em.  There might
be a reward afterwards...

